{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implementation will be developed in Go, targeting Hyperledger Fabric's modular channel configuration API/SDK structures.",
    "Functions will maintain immutability and functional option patterns consistent with existing Fabric config transaction manipulation libraries.",
    "Certificate revocation (U8) will utilize standard Go crypto/x509 package to validate certificate signatures against MSP root and intermediate CA certificates before updating the FabricMSPConfig revocation list.",
    "Policy management helpers (U2-U4) will support mutating both implicit meta policies and signature policies at organizational and group levels."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Development takes place within an existing Go codebase dedicated to Fabric channel configuration (e.g., fabric-config).",
    "Protobuf definitions and core data models for channel configurations and MSPs are already defined and available.",
    "Developer is responsible for design, implementation, unit testing, updating example tests, and documentation.",
    "One workday represents 8 hours of dedicated development effort."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements Analysis & API Design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze existing channel configuration data structures and design function signatures for org retrieval, policy modification, org addition, MSP extraction, and cert revocation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Org Configuration Retrieval (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Implement API functions to inspect and extract config.Organization structures for Application, Orderer, and Consortium orgs from a channel configuration transaction.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-3",
      "activity_name": "Implement Policy Modification Helpers (U2, U3, U4)",
      "activity_description": "Develop functions to add and remove policies for Application, Orderer, and Consortium orgs and groups, returning modified configuration transactions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-4",
      "activity_name": "Implement Orderer and Application Org Addition Functions (U5, U6)",
      "activity_description": "Develop fit-for-purpose functions to append new Orderer org and Application org definitions to channel configuration transactions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-5",
      "activity_name": "Implement MSP Config Retrieval (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Implement helper function to extract MSP configuration details for a specified org directly from the config transaction without manual parsing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-6",
      "activity_name": "Implement Certificate Revocation & MSP Verification (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Develop function to verify certificate issuance against MSP CA certs and append valid serial/SKI to the FabricMSPConfig revocation_list, returning errors for unissued certs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-7",
      "activity_name": "Unit Testing & Example Updates",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for all new helper functions and update example tests across U1-U8 to demonstrate usage patterns.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-8",
      "activity_name": "Code Review, Linting & Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Perform self-review, run linters and static checks, document exported functions, and finalize the pull request.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 10.5
  }
}
```

